  "diagnostic_only": true,
  "diagnostic_reason": "the spread level month by month for a population fixed by the published group list, plus each venue's Appendix B coverage. Written because every other reading in this stage is a difference between two windows and a difference cannot say whether one of its windows is unusual. B14 stage two is locked, so this is evidence and not a licensed reading",
  "findings": [
    "The two venues' Appendix B coverage is not comparable across 201804. Venue N runs 969 distinct symbols in 201608 (pre-pilot, whole market), 687 from 201610 (the pilot universe), decays to 618 by 201803, and then jumps to 2110 in 201804. Venue P runs 3097, 2396, 2135, 2126 across the same points. From 201804 onward the two are identical to a handful (2071 and 2071 in 201809), where before it venue N carried about thirty per cent of what venue P carried. So what changed in 201804 is venue N's reporting scope, not the market. The names that appear are Nasdaq-listed (AAOI, AAON, ABAX, ABCB, ACIW, ACOR) and the group proportions are preserved, so the change is not selective by group",
    "The entry round therefore reads about 679 venue-N symbols and the exit round about 2070, and roughly two thirds of the exit round's population is Nasdaq-listed names whose venue-N activity is marginal. That is a candidate explanation for the whole difference in behaviour between the rounds: thin activity gives noisy spreads and noisy spreads are what make an answer turn on the weighting convention. It is a candidate and not a finding until the exit round is re-run on the pre-201804 population",
    "The entry round's own two windows also straddle a coverage change, 201610, where the file narrows from the whole market to the pilot universe. That one does not corrupt it: deltas requires a symbol in both windows, so the population is the intersection, and gate0's record of 679 venue-N symbols matches the narrower post-window scope",
    "The entry round reads 2016 windows and the exit round reads 2018 windows, so they sit on opposite sides of that coverage change and are not the same instrument on the same securities. Nothing that compares the two rounds directly can ignore it",
    "From 201604 to 201803 the venue N control level stays between -2.4406 and -2.2021, a range of 0.24 over two years. From 201810 to 201903 it runs -1.8161, -1.1970, -1.4564, -1.2008, -1.6455, -1.7590, a swing of 0.62 in six months, and November and January are more extreme than December although December was the worse month for the market",
    "So the exit round has no clean post window, and the reason is a property of this data after the pilot ended rather than one quarter's market conditions. October reads clean because it is the last month before the swing begins, and it has already moved from -1.93 to -1.82",
    "The pre window is not the anomaly. An earlier reading of this stage guessed that it was, on the grounds that two post windows a quarter apart gave the same control delta. The level series shows 201808 and 201809 flat against each other and against the months before them, and the instability entirely after them. That guess was wrong and is recorded as wrong"
  ],
